+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board. Committed changes are pushed to browsers over WebSockets served by the board's own infrastructure: the change store records each committed edit as a replayable revision, delivery publishes revisions to connected socket sessions and manages those sessions, and a browser that reconnects catches up by replaying revisions newer than the last one it applied. This keeps updates fast without a realtime vendor; in exchange, the board owns its connection capacity, session management, and reconnect behavior.
 
